# Background processes on Windows

Mu owns every Bash call and its descendants through a Windows Job Object.
`setsid`, `nohup`, shell backgrounding, and detached subprocess flags do not
allow ordinary descendants to outlive that call. Do not improvise an escape.

Run delegated work synchronously with a suitable timeout. Persistent services
must be started and owned outside Mu, for example in another user-controlled
terminal. Report this requirement and let the user arrange that lifetime.
